//
// PROBE: the terminal words, as a capture sees them.
//
// bund.prompt is a fixed string with fixed colour codes
// (Bund/src/stdlib/functions/io/input.rs:14-18). io.banner draws with cfonts'
// tiny font and always answers on the stack
// (Bund/src/stdlib/functions/io/banner.rs:36-43). The capture gives a program
// no input, so input and input* meet end-of-file at once: input pushes
// nothing, and input* runs its lambda on nothing (input.rs:46-51,117-124).
//
"probe: bund.prompt" println
bund.prompt println
"probe: io.banner draws a string" println
"Bund" io.banner println
"probe: io.banner. converts a number and takes it from the workbench" println
42 . io.banner. println
"probe: input at end of input pushes nothing" println
"? " input
"probe: input* at end of input never runs its lambda" println
"? " { "never" println } input*
"done" println
